---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { getTranslations } from "../../i18n";

const lang = "en";
const t = getTranslations(lang);
---

<LegalLayout
  title={t.meta.termsTitle}
  description="SliceBill Terms of Service — rules and conditions for using the app."
  lang={lang}
  lastUpdated="May 30, 2025"
>
  <h2>1. About SliceBill</h2>
  <p>
    SliceBill is an expense-splitting application developed and operated by <strong>DARDAN SP. Z O.O.</strong> (ul. Lewandowskiej 68, 43-143 Lędziny, Poland; NIP: 6462933321; KRS: 0000497120). SliceBill helps groups track shared expenses and calculate who owes what.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>SliceBill is not a financial service, a payment processor, or a bank.</strong> The app performs calculations only — it does not move money, hold funds, or execute transactions.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, installing, or using SliceBill, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, do not use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least <strong>13 years old</strong> to use SliceBill. By using the app, you confirm that you meet this age requirement. If you are under 18, you represent that you have parental consent.
  </p>

